{"archetypes":[{"name":"harness-pin-accuracy","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan cites very specific line numbers and exact string literals for five test-design-structure.sh assertions; if those references are stale or misquoted, CI will silently diverge from the prose change.","prompt_body":"Verify that every exact string literal the plan proposes to search-and-replace in scripts/test-design-structure.sh actually appears verbatim at the cited line numbers in the current file. Check whether the five `contains` assertion strings (old and new) match the current file content byte-for-byte, including backtick vs. smart-quote discrepancies and surrounding whitespace. Also confirm that the plan's 'byte-stable' claims for lines ~60, ~88, ~89, and ~597 are accurate by reading those lines directly. If any cited literal is absent or shifted, identify the actual current wording so the implementer can correct the plan before touching the file. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"routing-label-sweep","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan claims a repo-wide grep found exactly five 'passive-summary Continue' occurrences; if any were missed, a dangling reference to the now-removed option name survives in the shipped skill surface.","prompt_body":"Search skills/design/SKILL.md and skills/design/references/approval-gates.md for every occurrence of the phrase 'passive-summary Continue' (case-sensitive) and verify the plan accounts for all of them — neither fewer nor more than the five spots it enumerates (approval-gates lines ~100 and ~168; SKILL.md lines ~1106, ~1117, ~1145). Also check for the phrase 'Continue to Step 3.6 and Gate C' in the same two files to confirm the plan's claim that this wording disappears entirely after the change. Flag any occurrence that the plan does not mention, including occurrences inside quoted examples or nested sub-bullets that a line-number scan might skip. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
